    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d648">

                <pb facs="0882" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.6363 African Exploration and Development
                    Corp./3: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-09-02T13:00:00+02:35">September 2,
                            1935—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 2—12:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>86. My 84, August 30, noon. In reply to questions from my colleagues and the
                    press I have consistently maintained the concession was a purely commercial
                    matter without any political significance whatever and that neither the American
                    Government nor this Legation had taken part in the negotiations. I should be
                    glad to have the Department’s approval and guidance.</p>
                <p>I understand Rickett, who signed on behalf of the company, tried also to obtain
                    contract for Lake Tsana project but was referred to the White
                        Corporation.<anchor n="95" xml:id="d648-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d648-f1" n="95" xml:id="d648-f1-content">
                <p>The J. G. White Engineering Corporation, of New York.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
